<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pandit Seu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1680–c. 1740</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pandit Seu was an Indian painter from Guler in the hills of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>, active in the early 18th century. He headed a family workshop of painters, and his sons <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manaku">Manaku</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nainsukh">Nainsukh</a>, together with their own sons, transformed Pahari painting and created the style later known as Kangra painting.</p></div>
